{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ומקנה רב היה", :translit "u-mikneh rav hayah", :gloss "and much cattle was"} {:he "לבני ראובן ולבני גד", :translit "li-vnei re'uven u-li-vnei gad", :gloss "to the sons of Reuben and to the sons of Gad"} {:he "ואמר בני גד ובני ראובן", :translit "va-yomru bnei gad u-vnei re'uven", :gloss "and the sons of Gad and the sons of Reuben said"} {:he "וטרף זרוע אף קדקד", :translit "va-taraf zero'a af kodkod", :gloss "and he tore the arm also the crown of the head"} {:he "נחלה מבוהלת בראשונה ואחריתה לא תבורך", :translit "nahalah mevohellet ba-rishonah ve-achritah lo tevorach", :gloss "a hasty inheritance at first, its end shall not be blessed"} {:he "מבוהלת", :translit "mevohellet", :gloss "hasty"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 8, :occurrences ["בני גד ובני ראובן"]} {:kind :other, :note "The word מבוהלת is read as if written מבוחלת (with ḥet instead of heh), linking the ḥet (numerical 8) to the 8 mentions and 8 years of early exile."}], :frame {:text "The verse Deuteronomy 33:20–21 describes Gad's portion: 'Blessed be He that enlargetes Gad… he came at the head of the people' — understood as Gad leading in battle. Deuteronomy 33:6 says of Reuben, 'Let Reuben live and not die,' and Genesis 49:3 calls Reuben 'the firstborn.' The phrase 'a hasty inheritance at first, its end shall not be blessed' (נחלה מבוהלת בראשונה ואחריתה לא תבורך) appears in Proverbs 20:21. 1 Chronicles 5:26 records that the Transjordan tribes — Reuben, Gad, and the half-tribe of Manasseh — were exiled by the king of Assyria before the other tribes.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 33:20–21" "Deuteronomy 33:6" "Genesis 49:3" "Proverbs 20:21" "1 Chronicles 5:26"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 8, :occurrences ["בני גד ובני ראובן"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "בני גד ובני ראובן", :refs ["Numbers 32:2" "Numbers 32:25" "Numbers 32:29" "Numbers 32:31"], :n 4, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "The word מבוהלת is read as if written מבוחלת (with ḥet instead of heh), linking the ḥet (numerical 8) to the 8 mentions and 8 years of early exile.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:32:25.379852844Z", :model "glm-5.2"}